# Files excluded from the published package.
#
# This file is **required**, not optional: `dart pub publish` falls back to
# `.gitignore` when `.pubignore` is absent, and `.gitignore` does not mention
# `.agents/` in a way that survives the switch. Since `.agents/` holds complete
# copies of this crate (the isolated verification workspaces), shipping it would
# turn a ~1 MB package into tens of megabytes of duplicated source.
#
# Every pattern is rooted with a leading `/`. That is deliberate and it is the
# single most expensive lesson in this project's history: an unanchored `build/`
# matches at *any* depth, so it silently deletes `lib/src/build/`, and an
# unanchored `wasmtime/` deleted a whole `lib/src/wasmtime/` API layer. The
# package published fine and did not compile for anyone. Written as `/build/`,
# the same pattern only ever matches the package root.
#
# `.github/scripts/check_archive.dart` asserts the consequence of getting this
# wrong: it unpacks the dry-run archive and fails if any library is incomplete.

# --- the agent's own workspace, never shipped -------------------------------
/.agents/
/.oxideav-research/

# --- build output and caches ------------------------------------------------
/.dart_tool/
/build/
/coverage/
/doc/api/
/rust/target/
/example/.dart_tool/
/example/build/
/example/coverage/
/example/.flutter-plugins
/example/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
/example/linux/flutter/ephemeral/
/example/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/
/example/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
/example/ios/Flutter/ephemeral/

# --- editor and OS noise ----------------------------------------------------
/.vscode/
/.idea/
**/*.iml
.DS_Store

# --- lockfiles ---------------------------------------------------------------
# A Dart library must not pin its consumers, so the pubspec locks stay out. The
# Rust lock is the opposite case: the build hook compiles a cdylib whose
# dependency versions should not drift under a consumer's feet, so it ships.
/pubspec.lock
/example/pubspec.lock
